        "id": "intro-comment",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Emboss a Still\n\nTurns an image into a relief effect. Emboss reads brightness changes rather than colour, so flat areas go grey and only the edges stand out.\n\n**How it works:** \"Image\" passes the picture to \"Emboss\", which applies the relief filter. \"Result\" shows the embossed image. It is local pixel processing with no model or key.\n\n**Try this:** Run it on a photo with strong outlines, such as architecture or text on a sign, and compare it with a soft portrait to see how much the effect depends on edges."
        },
